  "approvalStatus": "unapproved",
  "note": "What size of change in a parameter is worth a clinician's attention, in the parameter's own canonical unit. Bands are ABSOLUTE, never percentage: a 20 percent fall in sodium and a 20 percent fall in heart rate are not the same event, and a percentage rule makes the two indistinguishable. 'concern' names the direction worth telling somebody about, and is used only for ranking; a change in the other direction is still reported. 'rank' breaks ties between changes of the same band so the order is stable and reviewable rather than incidental. UNAPPROVED seed content: these are engineering defaults for a display, they gate nothing, and the clinical lead owns the values.",
